{"title":"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(some_guessing_involved)/&quot;Engineer&#39;s_Induction&quot;\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (some guessing involved)/\"Engineer's Induction\"</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(if_you_did_not_know_how_to_use_the_numbers_given_in_the_problem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (if you did not know how to use the numbers given in the problem)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sequence\" title=\"Sequence\">sequence</a> is defined as follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883bfac4b2a2f2829b6ed4cb1a3098a56dd698a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=a_2=a_3=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" /> and, for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26b7df8e18eaf3f836d5ff1f52e66f1395bf4355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n, a_{n+3}=a_{n+2}+a_{n+1}+a_n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"14\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f0d1ab806661a1cf83f8ffd89c52ba8aa86b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{28}=6090307, a_{29}=11201821,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"244\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b45e20baed958a76e97f7df60c49a5fc15023266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{30}=20603361,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Remainder\" title=\"Remainder\">remainder</a> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245bf6a267dad3fcccea3f85f48b8a3ebe4b2f40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum^{28}_{k=1} a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"45\" height=\"50\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define the sum as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d1c95bbbf27c5d26f78db9420adb1b8b1ceb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n\\ = a_{n + 3} - a_{n + 2} - a_{n + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"12\" />, the sum will be:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/d/2ad278b512318ab58fc7ef7280e03bd129453fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = a_{28} + \\sum^{27}_{k=1} (a_{k+3}-a_{k+2}-a_{k+1}) \\\\ s = a_{28} + \\left(\\sum^{30}_{k=4} a_{k} - \\sum^{29}_{k=3} a_{k}\\right) - \\left(\\sum^{28}_{k=2} a_{k}\\right)\\\\ s = a_{28} + (a_{30} - a_{3}) - \\left(\\sum^{28}_{k=2} a_{k}\\right) = a_{28} + a_{30} - a_{3} - (s - a_{1})\\\\ s = -s + a_{28} + a_{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"468\" height=\"178\" /></center>\n<p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6335fb21b152db73bff219b2200e719f8af15b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{a_{28} + a_{30}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"105\" height=\"35\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf96d4d3d1981a8e9277b8c05a4c9ac162695e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{28},\\,a_{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"11\" /> are both given; the last four digits of their sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/1263e9c144b2e464df84c556f4aaaa675329ea7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3668$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, and half of that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e01dfbe36900bd6296a9d6928df541495d8cebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1834$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9df3fc4b66a1203b60ef68f2fb46fbb5485f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{834}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.−\t\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(bash)\">Solution 2 (bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since the problem only asks for the first 28 terms and we only need to calculate mod 1000, we simply bash the first 28 terms:\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c6412981926490b0aa83da78fc7f1f158222be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}\\equiv 1 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{2}\\equiv 1 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{3}\\equiv 1 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{4}\\equiv 3 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{5}\\equiv 5 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{6}\\equiv 9 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{7}\\equiv 17 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{8}\\equiv 31 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{9}\\equiv 57 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{10}\\equiv 105 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{11}\\equiv 193 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{12}\\equiv 355 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{13}\\equiv 653 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{14}\\equiv 201 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{15}\\equiv 209 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{16}\\equiv 63 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{17}\\equiv 473 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{18}\\equiv 745 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{19}\\equiv 281 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{20}\\equiv 499 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{21}\\equiv 525 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{22}\\equiv 305 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{23}\\equiv 329 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{24}\\equiv 159 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{25} \\equiv 793 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{26} \\equiv 281 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{27} \\equiv 233 \\pmod {1000} \\\\ a_{28} \\equiv 307 \\pmod {1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"558\" />\n</p><p>Adding all the residues shows the sum is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9df3fc4b66a1203b60ef68f2fb46fbb5485f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{834}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~ I-_-I\n</p><p>~ flyingkinder123 (values for bash)\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28some_guessing_involved.29.2F.22Engineer.27s_Induction.22\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(some_guessing_involved)/&quot;Engineer's_Induction&quot;\">Solution 3 (some guessing involved)/\"Engineer's Induction\"</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (some guessing involved)/&quot;Engineer&#39;s Induction&quot;\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>All terms in the sequence are sums of previous terms, so the sum of all terms up to a certain point must be some linear combination of the first three terms. Also, we are given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c765e5218352508630c2cc90999f6a88317e8cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{28}, a_{29},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b0f05c1ff50dd0935567e47d49625bba858415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" />, so we can guess that there is some way to use them in a formula. Namely, we guess that there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/48689d638ddca59030006d362cbd848607f63aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p, q, r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f947d58f352b010d2a4cad4ed537862997d3c590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n}{a_k} = pa_n+qa_{n+1}+ra_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"229\" height=\"48\" />. From here, we list out the first few terms of the sequence and the cumulative sums, and with a little bit of substitution and algebra we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d4dd0729b7c3cc16e594d9744a216ba2fc4b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p, q, r) = (\\frac{1}{2}, 0, \\frac{1}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"145\" height=\"37\" />, at least for the first few terms. From this, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf80fbb4a46304016f2bacc229bebfa8318097d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{28}{a_k} = \\frac{a_{28}+a_{30}}{2} \\equiv{\\boxed{834}}\\pmod {1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"308\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>Solution by zeroman; clarified by srisainandan6\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28if_you_did_not_know_how_to_use_the_numbers_given_in_the_problem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(if_you_did_not_know_how_to_use_the_numbers_given_in_the_problem)\">Solution 4 (if you did not know how to use the numbers given in the problem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (if you did not know how to use the numbers given in the problem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the Chinese remainder theorem, each number under 1000 is uniquely determined by its mod 8 and mod 125.\n</p><p>We list a few terms of the sequence mod 8:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7d16b18aebc3c07295292dde0ab74c5fe6f13c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1,1,1,3,5,1,1,7,1,1,1,...\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the cycle repeats every 8 numbers, and each cycle has a sum of 4 mod 8. Therefore, the sum mod 8 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4f8f7e32f7bea2ff0407b98bdb5c6190798d6b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 \\cdot 4 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 3 = 2 \\mod 8.\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc67ac99edaf0c57aeff1bdc2336d616f858894.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s_n = \\sum _{i=1} ^{n} a_i.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"47\" /> It is easy to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b534741a214b4af71dc88a32bd30d3237b83411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{n+3} = s_{n+2} + s_{n+1} + s_{n}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>We write the sum (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24f09efdef5385985d3f51f9163958f3aaa64a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />) of the first terms mod 125:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f16807d15da1c8f023b35da861f45b927b8f9af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1,2,3,6,11,20,37,68,0,-20,48,28,56,7,91,29,2,-3,28,27,52,-18,61,-30,13,44,27,84.\\]\" width=\"713\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Therefore the desired number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737e66f7592440c366aebc5406c8dc470353229e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$84 \\mod 125.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>From here, we can determine the number we are looking for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38c2e027730ffd22da25a5831a1eb785c0096ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$750 + 84 = \\boxed{834}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"137\" height=\"25\" />\n-sd8\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II\" title=\"2006 AIME II\">2006 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2006 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017210335\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 239/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6882/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.283      1 -total\n 58.25%    7.155      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.27%    4.823      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5380:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017210335 and revision id 285095. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}